==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Grand Yokai Tengu''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Master Tengu''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Tengu is designed to counter [[Baron Seal]] and [[Archangel Exiel]], as its abilities make Tengu a good pick for those two [[Gauntlet]] bosses in particular. Keeping a decent distance from the boss with the ability to [[Knockback|knock it back]] occasionally helps keep the pressure off of your attackers. Outside of the two aforementioned [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] bosses, Cat Tengu is essentially your average specialist midranger, being a decent choice against its targets but also pretty replaceable. It does, however, have a cheap cost and fast recharge time for an Uber, so it can be a good pick on cash-tight stages.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Master Tengu provides a few small boosts; it gains higher health, Knockback chance and most notably, a more reliable Strengthen activation threshold, now activating at 50% health instead of 33% health. This makes it much safer to use in general, as it isn't prone to dying as easily whenever it tries to activate its [[Strengthen]]. The increased knockback chance makes it more consistent for pushing back enemies. Best of all, the evolution price is cheap for an Uber Super Rare, similar to many of the other Uber [[:Category:Colossus Slayer Cats|Colossus Slayers]].

Overall, a good True Form for the cost.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]]''' improves average DPS and also gives a 25% chance to stack with Knockback, allowing it to repeatedly hit enemies. While the spawn area is inconsistent, even one successful hit can massively relieve pressure from the very aggressive threats common among [[Red]] and [[Angel]] enemies. Also, the combination of Surge and Knockback is able to effectively ignore Sage Enemies’ resistance to debuffs thanks to the lingering hitbox of Surge Attacks continuously hitting them until they are out of the Surge entirely, regardless of the reduced push distance. This makes it a good counter to enemies like [[Doctor K.O.]], despite lacking [[Sage Slayer]].

'''[[Survive]]''' guarantees it will be able to use its Strengthen, and to attack for much longer with the increased power.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Slow]]''' is situational, as neither of his target Gauntlet bosses or their support have the [[Slow]] ability, and it is very rare among his other targets.

Attack Buff and HP Buff are good, compensating for the stat-based nature of the Gauntlets associated with his targets, thus giving his Strengthen much better reliability.

