==Trivia==
*Cat Tengu is based on ''[[wikipedia:Tengu|tengu]]'', a class of bird-like ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' in Japanese mythology. The staff it wields is a [[wikipedia:Khakkhara|khakkhara]], a metal-ringed staff used by Buddhist monks and many depictions of ''tengu''.
**''Tengu'' are one of the few ''yōkai'' to have appeared in all three of [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' major tower defense titles ([[The Battle Cats]] and the more ''yōkai''-focused [[Kyoutou Project]] and [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]]). The others are ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'', ''[[wikipedia:Kitsune|kitsune]]'', ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'' and ''[[wikipedia:Nekomata|nekomata]]'', which appear in The Battle Cats as [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]], [[Trickster Himeyuri (Uber Rare Cat)|Trickster Himeyuri]], [[Kappy Jr.]] and the cats floating beside [[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]], respectively.
***Out of the three games, The Battle Cats is the only one in which ''tengu'' are never fought as enemies.
**Cat Tengu is the second ''tengu''-based [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]], the first being [[Karasu-Tengu Tenten (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Karasu-Tengu Tenten]].

